s it's the biggest threat in the  country do you feel that in your daily  life  i feel and many friends tell me that  we are more afraid of being jewish in  germany today  than we have been half a year ago or a  year ago  this trend started to rise a couple of  years ago  um being uh  being forced by the platforms by social  media where anti-semitic conspiracy  theories  thrive uh so the attack on halo  was not a surprise to many we were  rather expecting  when will something happen and where  will something happen  and we are expecting the next terror  attacks today  as the likes of q anon spread around the  globe telling anti-semitic conspiracy  theories  that certainly is alarming i mean it's  been a year since the attack  now in hala has germany been doing  enough  i don't think that germany has been  doing enough we are particularly  concerned with  the far-right extremist views within the  police because whenever i receive death  threats or  rape threats what i do is i go to the  police  but we are now learning of more and more  police stations  where right wing radical chats  groups preparation groups have been  uncovered  and the ministers of the interior aren't  doing a very good job  at uncovering these structures on the  contrary they are saying that we do not  need studies because the police has no  problem of racism and uh the synagogues  aren't protected well enough  and where they are um the uh  minister president has uh been saying  stalking  has been saying well the police are  needed elsewhere as well  and because we have to protect the jews  basically  we cannot react as fast to calls of the  police  from the other citizens well not doing  enough then  what do you say germany should be doing  to tackle the problem  i think that we need to look at the  larger structural issues that  is um antisemitic and racist structures  within the police  that is um what is going on on social  media monitor it more closely understand  these groups  more closely 